{
 "source": "This atlas's own audit of via: familysearch-catalogue places",
 "licence": "This atlas's own compilation",
 "note": "Thirty-six places promoted from FamilySearch collection records that cannot be right, removed on 16 October 2026. Each exists only because of the lookup that commit 38268ef fixed on 20 September: it read a collection's place ids through /places/reps/, a different numbering, and got back an unrelated row with HTTP 200 — Mindarie, New South Wales, for the Caribbean. The promoter ran on those answers, and nothing re-checked the places it had already written. The test that found them: the place's country is not among the countries of the collection that claims it. 'Hong Kong' held North Carolina marriages; twenty-eight Australian localities held the Caribbean, Central America, Switzerland and the Isle of Man. Places that record their own filedUnder (Posen, Silesia, Pomerania, Viipuri, West Prussia) are historical filings, not errors, and were excluded. Kept here so a future harvest does not quietly put them back.",
